<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20138] FLR-EC: Reword "stripe set" to 'data stripe unit'</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20138</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Once the full EC series has landed, reword and harmonize terms like &lt;br/&gt;
stripe set -&amp;gt; data stripe unit&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;"&lt;br/&gt;
How does this terminology compare to existing RAID publications/implementations? As much as possible, we should use the same terminology to describe the EC implementation to minimize confusion. In &lt;a href="https://www.pdl.cmu.edu/PDL-FTP/Declustering/ASPLOS.pdf" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://www.pdl.cmu.edu/PDL-FTP/Declustering/ASPLOS.pdf&lt;/a&gt; it refers to this as a "data stripe unit", and has a "parity stripe unit" for the parity.&lt;br/&gt;
"&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This will touch a lot of different parts that are from different patches, many of which have not yet landed, so defer until they have all landed.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
